---
title: What's Next
description: Further resources for configuring feature flags and theming in the Vonage Video iOS App.
---

Congratulations! You have successfully configured feature flags and customized the theme for the Vonage Video iOS reference app using `app-config.json` and `semantics.json`.

## What You Accomplished

- Understood the structure of `VERA/Config/app-config.json`, including its `videoSettings`, `audioSettings`, `waitingRoomSettings`, and `meetingRoomSettings` sections
- Edited feature flags in `app-config.json` and regenerated `VERAConfiguration/VERAConfiguration/AppConfig.swift` with `generate-app-config.py`
- Understood the structure of `VERA/Theme/semantics.json`, including its color, `borderRadius`, and typography tokens
- Edited theme tokens in `semantics.json` and regenerated the `SemanticColors.xcassets` asset catalog with `generate-app-theme.py`
- Set up the shared backend connection by exporting `BASE_API_URL` and running `generateEnvironmentConstants.sh`
- Confirmed your changes by inspecting each generator script's terminal output and the generated Swift and asset catalog files, without building or running the app

## Resources

- [Vonage Developer Portal](https://developer.vonage.com) — Documentation, guides, and API references for all Vonage products.
- [Vonage Video API Documentation](https://developer.vonage.com/en/video/overview) — In-depth guides for the Video API.
- [vonage-video-ios-app on GitHub](https://github.com/Vonage/vonage-video-ios-app) — Source code, full README with all configuration options, and contribution guidelines.
